## Install Summary

PyTorch was installed from the `pytorch` and `nvidia` conda channels:

```bash
conda install -n bevfusion -y \
  pytorch==2.4.1 torchvision==0.19.1 torchaudio==2.4.1 pytorch-cuda=12.4 \
  -c pytorch -c nvidia
```

MPI and common Python dependencies:

```bash
conda install -n bevfusion -y -c conda-forge openmpi=4.0.4 mpi4py=3.0.3

conda run -n bevfusion pip install \
  Pillow==8.4.0 tqdm torchpack nuscenes-devkit numba==0.57.1 ninja \
  yapf==0.40.1 Cython
```

`mmcv-full` was built locally for the active PyTorch/CUDA stack:

```bash
MAX_JOBS=8 TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST="8.9;9.0" MMCV_WITH_OPS=1 FORCE_CUDA=1 \
  conda run -n bevfusion pip install --no-cache-dir --no-binary mmcv-full mmcv-full==1.7.2
```

MMDetection:

```bash
conda run -n bevfusion pip install mmdet==2.28.2 terminaltables pycocotools
```

## Custom CUDA Ops

The project still uses repository-local CUDA extensions. They are not CUDA built-ins. The compiled ops are defined in `setup.py`, including:

- `mmdet3d.ops.spconv.sparse_conv_ext`
- `mmdet3d.ops.bev_pool.bev_pool_ext`
- `mmdet3d.ops.feature_decorator.feature_decorator_ext`
- `mmdet3d.ops.iou3d.iou3d_cuda`
- `mmdet3d.ops.voxel.voxel_layer`
- `mmdet3d.ops.roiaware_pool3d.roiaware_pool3d_ext`
- `mmdet3d.ops.ball_query.ball_query_ext`
- `mmdet3d.ops.knn.knn_ext`
- `mmdet3d.ops.paconv.assign_score_withk_ext`
- `mmdet3d.ops.group_points.group_points_ext`
- `mmdet3d.ops.interpolate.interpolate_ext`
- `mmdet3d.ops.furthest_point_sample.furthest_point_sample_ext`
- `mmdet3d.ops.gather_points.gather_points_ext`

The CUDA arch list in `setup.py` was extended with:

```text
sm_89
sm_90
```

The repository extensions were rebuilt with:

```bash
MAX_JOBS=8 FORCE_CUDA=1 TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST="8.9;9.0" \
  conda run -n bevfusion python setup.py develop
```

## Code Compatibility Changes

The following compatibility updates were made for CUDA 12.4, PyTorch 2.4, and OpenMMLab 1.x:

- `setup.py`
  - Added `sm_89` and `sm_90` NVCC targets.
  - Added `feature_decorator_ext` to the compiled extension list.

- `mmdet3d/ops/feature_decorator/src/feature_decorator.cpp`
  - Changed PyTorch op registration integer flags from `int` to `bool`, because newer PyTorch only accepts `int64_t` and `bool` integral argument types for operator schemas.

- `mmdet3d/ops/spconv/conv.py`
  - Added `force=True` to sparse convolution registry decorators to avoid duplicate registration conflicts with newer `mmcv`.

- `mmdet3d/models/backbones/radar_encoder.py`
  - Made `flash_attn` optional. The camera+lidar detection config does not use this module path, but top-level imports previously required `flash_attn`.

- `mmdet3d/models/vtransforms/base.py`
  - Set `add_depth_features=False` by default so `DepthLSSTransform` matches the single-channel depth transform expected by the provided BEVFusion detection checkpoint.

- `tools/test.py`
  - Added a PyTorch 2.x compatibility patch for `mmcv.parallel._functions._get_stream`.
  - Added `_use_replicated_tensor_module = False` for `MMDistributedDataParallel`.
  - Passed `torch.device("cuda", current_device)` to the distributed wrapper.

Training uses `mmdet3d/apis/train.py`, so the same DDP/scatter compatibility needs to be present there before starting a full training run.

## Validation Result

The pretrained detection checkpoint was evaluated on local nuScenes val:

```bash
PATH="/root/miniconda3/envs/bevfusion/bin:$PATH" \
PYTHONPATH="/mnt/wfy/bevfusion:${PYTHONPATH:-}" \
/root/miniconda3/envs/bevfusion/bin/torchpack dist-run -np 4 -v \
  /root/miniconda3/envs/bevfusion/bin/python tools/test.py \
  configs/nuscenes/det/transfusion/secfpn/camera+lidar/swint_v0p075/convfuser.yaml \
  pretrained/bevfusion-det.pth \
  --eval bbox \
  --tmpdir /tmp/bevfusion_eval_tmp \
  --cfg-options model.encoders.camera.backbone.init_cfg.checkpoint=pretrained/swint-nuimages-pretrained.pth
```

