These are close to the README validation result for BEVFusion detection.

## Training Command

After applying the training DDP compatibility patch, use:

```bash
PATH="/root/miniconda3/envs/bevfusion/bin:$PATH" \
PYTHONPATH="/mnt/wfy/bevfusion:${PYTHONPATH:-}" \
/root/miniconda3/envs/bevfusion/bin/torchpack dist-run -np 4 -v \
  /root/miniconda3/envs/bevfusion/bin/python tools/train.py \
  configs/nuscenes/det/transfusion/secfpn/camera+lidar/swint_v0p075/convfuser.yaml \
  --run-dir runs/sm89_bevfusion_det \
  --model.encoders.camera.backbone.init_cfg.checkpoint pretrained/swint-nuimages-pretrained.pth \
  --load_from pretrained/lidar-only-det.pth \
  --optimizer_config.cumulative_iters 2
```

Current effective training settings for this config:

```text
num_gpus:        4
samples_per_gpu: 4
effective batch: 32
optimizer lr:    2.0e-4
max epochs:      6
```

`cumulative_iters=2` is used because the README fusion detection command is written for 8 GPUs with `samples_per_gpu=4`. On 4 GPUs this keeps the effective global batch size close to the original training setup.
